WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:16.610
A seven-ship British fleet cuts into the pirate
bay of Nassau with imperial pomp, and fixes

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.430
its anchors into the seabed for the night.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:25.500
Captain Woodes Rogers had triumphantly arrived
to impose the will of His Royal Majesty King

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.920
George of Great Britain and Ireland.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.081
In the morning, he would tame this wretched
pirate haven ashore with sword and pistol,

00:00:33.081 --> 00:00:37.940
and finally cleanse it from scum and villainy.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.629
Night fell, and the crescent moon lights up the
deep ocean.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:50.969
There is the gentle creak of bending wood,
as two ships push off from the island.

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:53.960
The nearer ship sails directly toward Rogers.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.359
It heaves forward then bursts into flames.

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:04.860
The crew escape on cue, as shrapnel blisters
and spits in orange streaks over black waters.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.040
Crackling inferno spreads to one British ship,
and the others scatter in the frenzy.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.860
The fireship’s crew row to the second
vessel, and join their tenacious leader

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:20.900
- the ruthless pirate who deigns to defy
the King: Charles Vane.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:29.140
Woodes Rogers watches him escape into the
smoldering, tropical night.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:35.920
Vane understood perfectly well why Rogers

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.110
and the civilized world wanted to see him
hang: theft, torture, and murder were sins

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.320
to which he shamelessly admitted.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:48.451
He reserved less sympathy for the scores of
pirates who had betrayed him - indeed, many

00:01:48.451 --> 00:01:52.800
men he knew had stayed behind to welcome Woodes
Rogers into Nassau.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.060
They had elected to accept this [b]so-called
King’s pardon.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.140
But Vane had taken his chances.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:04.020
He was no coward, and wouldn´t give up his
paradise that easily.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.890
Nassau, which constituted the island of New
Providence in the Caribbean, had fallen out

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.039
of British hands some years ago.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:17.290
Its winding farmlands and cobwebbed cannons
duly became the property of Charles Vane,

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.700
Blackbeard, Benjamin Hornigold, and thousands
of other pirates.[c]

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:26.569
Together, they had fashioned the island into
a Republic of Pirates, from which to plunder

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:32.520
this corner of the Atlantic, a liminal anarchy
between English, Spanish and French dominions.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.819
But so great were their spoils, that those
royal dynasties of Europe fretted upon their

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:43.739
thrones and decried the unkempt outlaws who
so wantonly emptied their treasuries.

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:49.530
And so, Woodes Rogers had thus been tasked
with their extermination.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:54.670
Despite Charles Vane’s fiery attack, Rogers
successfully made landfall the next morning.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:03:01.010
He pardoned every pacified pirate ashore and
raised the Union Jack atop the dusty fort.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.780
The hunt for the others who roamed these seas
was already underway.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:10.180
Those who persisted in their thievery were
brought back to Nassau and walked to the gallows

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:15.019
in front of their former shipmates who had
accepted the pardon.

00:03:15.019 --> 00:03:18.470
Woodes Rogers sat as governor of Nassau.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:29.069
This seemed a momentous occasion - an age
of order was upon them.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:32.909
If Charles Vane, Blackbeard, and the other
stragglers dared to resist, they would have

00:03:32.909 --> 00:03:37.409
a front row seat to the end of their way of
life.

00:03:37.409 --> 00:03:41.840
And indeed, this appeared to be the death
of a people who had long thrived like mold

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:47.340
on the dark underbellies of celebrated empires,
a people whose bloodstained legacy of freedom

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.989
and butchery and rebellion began eons before.

00:03:50.989 --> 00:03:56.209
A proud history of piracy millenia long preceded
these men.

00:03:56.209 --> 00:04:03.569
From empire toppling flotillas to singular
scoundrels and back again - this is their

00:04:03.569 --> 00:04:04.569
story.

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:10.631
This is the story of the Pirates of the West.

00:04:20.825 --> 00:04:27.830
Pirates didn't really have schools. They're training was mainly from their previous
lives as legitimate seafolk - taking their

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.900
previous sailing skills and using them to
their advantage.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:37.400
These days its harder to do this so directly
- so services like Skillshare are hugely helpful

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.310
